Step-0 perf telemetry for the Android port (see NATIVE_PLAN.md).

Upstream ships a perf-counter registry (rex::perf::CounterId) but compiles it
out of Release builds and only placed PROFILE_ callsites in the D3D12
backend. This patch:

1. Enables REXGLUE_ENABLE_PERF_COUNTERS unconditionally (relaxed atomics,
   ~1 ns per hit; Tracy stays compiled out in Release).
2. Mirrors the D3D12 PROFILE_ callsites into the Vulkan backend:
   - draws + vertices at host draw record (primitive path only, like D3D12;
     the 3-vertex resolve helper draw is not counted),
   - pipeline cache hit/miss in EnsurePipelineCreated,
   - texture object hit/miss in the shared FindOrCreateTexture (measures
     upload churn; D3D12 builds would add descriptor-level hits on top of
     this, but nothing builds D3D12 with counters),
   - command-buffer stall on the blocking fence wait (not the zero-timeout
     poll).
   Freebies already wired upstream and now live in Release: frame time/FPS
   (Flip), dispatcher + interrupt counts, XMA frames, audio queue depth.
   Deliberately NOT wired (no cheap seam): APC depth (intrusive list walk),
   thread create/exit (rare), audio latency, critical-region contention.
3. Adds an Android perf-timeline tick to the Vulkan presenter: every present
   accumulates the last flipped frame's snapshot; every 300 presents one
   WARN-level PERFDATA line with averages goes to the shared log (WARN:
   presets run warning+, so INFO would never be seen; ultra stays quiet).
   Presents without an intervening guest-frame Flip re-add the same
   snapshot; negligible at the steady-state 1:1 present/frame ratio.

